:: StoryStylesheet [stylesheet]
@import url("styles/the-glass-orchard.css");

tw-story {
  background: #071311;
  color: #edf4ed;
  font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 100vh;
  width: 100%;
}

tw-passage {
  display: block;
  margin: 0;
  max-width: none;
  padding: 0;
}

.orchard-scene {
  align-items: center;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  display: flex;
  min-height: 100vh;
  overflow: hidden;
  padding: 2rem 6vw;
  position: relative;
}

.orchard-scene__art {
  filter: brightness(.56) saturate(.82);
  height: 100%;
  inset: 0;
  object-fit: cover;
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
}

.orchard-scene::after {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(3, 14, 13, .96) 0%, rgba(4, 17, 15, .88) 34%, rgba(5, 17, 16, .34) 68%, rgba(5, 12, 13, .12) 100%);
  content: "";
  inset: 0;
  position: absolute;
}

.orchard-card {
  backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(10, 30, 27, .86), rgba(7, 20, 19, .7));
  border: 1px solid rgba(151, 216, 190, .22);
  border-left: 3px solid #d0a65b;
  box-shadow: 0 28px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, .38);
  max-width: 39rem;
  padding: 1.5rem 2.25rem 1.4rem;
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
}

.orchard-kicker,
.orchard-time {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  letter-spacing: .22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.orchard-kicker {
  color: #d0a65b;
  font-size: .72rem;
  margin-bottom: .55rem;
}

.orchard-time {
  color: #8bd6bf;
  font-size: .82rem;
  margin-bottom: .85rem;
}

.orchard-card h1 {
  color: #f2f2e9;
  font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 3vw, 3.45rem);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: -.035em;
  line-height: .96;
  margin: 0 0 .9rem;
}

.orchard-card p {
  color: #cbd8d2;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  margin: 0 0 .9rem;
  max-width: 34rem;
}

.orchard-links {
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(151, 216, 190, .16);
  display: grid;
  gap: .25rem;
  padding-top: .6rem;
}

.orchard-links tw-link {
  color: #96dec7;
  font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
  font-size: .94rem;
  font-weight: 650;
  letter-spacing: .01em;
  padding: .35rem 0;
}

.orchard-links tw-link::after {
  color: #d0a65b;
  content: "  →";
}

.orchard-links tw-link:hover {
  color: #f1c875;
}

:: StoryScript [script]
console.info("Glass Orchard preview ready");

:: Arrival [opening glasshouse] {"position":"80,280","size":"210,130"}
(set: $light to false)(set: $key to false)(set: $rain to "silver")
<div class="orchard-scene">
  <img class="orchard-scene__art" src="assets/orchard-atrium.jpg" alt="">
  <section class="orchard-card">
    <div class="orchard-kicker">The Glass Orchard</div>
    <div class="orchard-time">North Glasshouse · 03:17</div>
    <h1>The orchard remembers every visitor.</h1>
    <p>Rain maps the roof in silver veins. Beyond the fogged panes, a brass bell rings once—and a door that was not there yesterday stands open.</p>
    <div class="orchard-links">
      [[Enter the greenhouse->Greenhouse]]
      [[Follow the service stairs->Service Stairs]]
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

:: Greenhouse [glasshouse hub] {"position":"360,140","size":"210,130"}
(set: $light to true)
The old citrus trees turn their leaves toward your lamp. Beneath the western bench, a line of wet footprints disappears into the wall.

[[Climb toward the observatory->Observatory]]

[[Cross the glass gallery->Glass Gallery]]

:: Service Stairs [west-wing] {"position":"360,440","size":"210,130"}
The iron stairs answer each step with a different note. One landing smells of dust; the next, of fresh rain.

[[Try the archive door->Archive]]

[[Descend to the root cellar->Root Cellar]]

:: Archive [west-wing clue] {"position":"660,440","size":"210,130"}
(set: $key to true)
<img src="assets/archive-key.jpg" alt="A brass archive key beside a constellation plate">

The missing ledger has left a clean rectangle in the dust. In its place lies a warm brass key engraved with a map of unfamiliar stars.

[[Take the tower stair->Bell Tower]]

[[Open the sealed room->Locked Annex]]

:: Observatory [east-wing clue] {"position":"660,140","size":"210,130"}
<img src="assets/constellation-plate.svg" alt="The orchard constellation plate">

The telescope is aimed below the horizon. Its brass setting reads //ORCHARD, WINTER QUARTER//.

[[Ring the brass bell->Bell Tower]]

[[Follow the star map outside->Night Garden]]

:: Glass Gallery [east-wing] {"position":"970,240","size":"210,130"}
Portraits of vanished gardeners hang between the windows. Every painted eye is fixed on the same patch of moonlit soil.

[[Compare the observatory records->Observatory]]

[[Step into the night garden->Night Garden]]

:: Root Cellar [west-wing clue] {"position":"970,440","size":"210,130"}
The roots have grown around a tin dispatch case without crushing it. Inside: one torn page from the archive ledger.

[[Return the page to the archive->Archive]]

[[Follow the roots outside->Night Garden]]

:: Bell Tower [tower] {"position":"970,60","size":"210,130"}
The bell rope is wet. When you pull it, every greenhouse lamp wakes at once and the observatory door opens below.

[[Walk toward the eastern gate->Departure]]

:: Night Garden [garden hub] {"position":"1280,250","size":"210,130"}
<img src="assets/moonflower-specimen.jpg" alt="A moonflower specimen plate">

Moonflowers unfold across the old paths, each transparent petal holding a different reflection of the glasshouse.

[[Leave by the eastern gate->Departure]]

[[Return beneath the glass->Greenhouse]]

:: Departure [ending] {"position":"1580,250","size":"210,130"}
At dawn, the gate stands where it always did. The brass key in your pocket is warm, and one impossible flower has opened beside the road.

[[Begin again->Arrival]]
